# Copy to .env.local for local development. None of these are required to run locally.

# --- Login -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave PRD_PASSWORD unset locally and the app runs with no login, as designed.
# Setting it is REQUIRED for any deployment: without it the app refuses to serve,
# rather than sitting on the public internet as an open read-write database.
# PRD_USERNAME=admin
# PRD_PASSWORD=
# Signs session cookies. Set it separately so changing the password does not have
# to sign everyone out, and vice versa. Defaults to PRD_PASSWORD if unset.
# PRD_SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Storage -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset: a local SQLite file at data/prd.db, exactly as the brief described.
# Set: Postgres, for platforms with no persistent disk. On Supabase use the
# TRANSACTION pooler string (port 6543), which is the one built for serverless.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# Overrides where the local SQLite file lives. The test suite uses this.
# PRD_DB_PATH=data/prd.db

# --- Deployment --------------------------------------------------------------
# Stops npm downloading a 170MB browser during the build. Serverless uses
# @sparticuz/chromium instead. Set this on Vercel; leave it unset locally.
# PUPPETEER_SKIP_DOWNLOAD=1
